  "title": "A and B",
  "summary": "The last two letters, and the seven-letter alphabet that names every white key.",
  "minutes": 5,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "A, B and back to C",
      "body": "Inside the group of three black keys, after F and G, come **A** and **B**. Then the next C starts again. These seven letters, A B C D E F G, are the **musical alphabet**. There is no H: after G it goes back to A.\n\n**Why it matters:** With only seven letters, you can now name every white key on the piano. Going up, the letters go forward. Going down, they go backward.",
